        <mxCell id="alternative" value="INTER-REGION OPTION&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Global VNet peering can connect hubs, but it does not form a BGP session or automatically provide spoke-to-spoke transit." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=14;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="346" width="200" height="180" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wave" value="WAVE 1  /  MOVE THE ROUTED /17&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Keep the West Europe cluster for rollback, but disconnect its spoke and confirm the old route is withdrawn.&lt;br&gt;2. Connect the Israel spoke and confirm Israel is the only origin for that /17. Check what on-prem, GCP, and West Europe select.&lt;br&gt;3. Validate private DNS, app VIP and TLS, Sweden Foundry access, and symmetric firewall inspection. Blob and Key Vault stay on Private Link." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacing=16;fontSize=15;fillColor=#f0f9f4;strokeColor=#528d61;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="405" y="742" width="610" height="208" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
